    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d947">

                <pb facs="0753" n="677" xml:id="pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/8175</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr.
                            Arredondo, representing American
                        interests</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-11-13T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 13, 1916, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>548. Department informed that authorities in Sonora in June, last, seized all
                    arms and ammunition belonging to American settlers at Esperanza and vicinity.
                    Settlers urgently need arms for protection against Yaqui Indians.</p>
                <p>Request appropriate authorities to order immediate return to settlers mentioned
                    of all arms and ammunition taken from them in June.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
